A1. What the present day is to the younger generation. ~ CHRISTMAS
A9. We're hearing a lot of talk from this now. ~ SCREEN
A11. This is what little Annie is. ~ ORPHAN
A14. This is a good one to cultivate and will help the market situation. ~ HOE
A15. A possessive pronoun. ~ ITS
A17. This has two banks in Paris. ~ SEINE
A18. Many an old bird has lost his freedom in this. ~ CAGE
A19. This was signed to the tune of "O Promise Me." ~ NOTE
A21. To separate. ~ SEVER
A23. This is part of one of Al Smith's addresses. (abbr.) ~ AV
A24. This is something farmers never like to grow. ~ OLD
A26. The gang way in Chicago. ~ RIDE
A27. Santa Claus put these in his own socks. ~ FEET
A30. The co-eds made a hit in this. ~ HOCKEY
A33. A lawyer's appendix. ~ LLD
A34. A margin ("of all sad words.") ~ EDGE
A35. Same. ~ ILK
A36. This comes at yawning. ~ NAP
A38. This kept high when everything was down on Wall Street. ~ EL
A39. A preserved peach. ~ GRANDMOTHER
A43. A small type. ~ EM
A45. A center position. ~ MID
A46. This is a terror. ~ AWE
A47. This is what the queen of hearts made. ~ TART
A49. A buggy outfit. ~ RIG
A51. What they did to the cruisers. ~ MOORED
A53. To give out. ~ EMIT
A54. It is hard to break this kind of a will. ~ IRON
A56. This puts everything around it in the shade. ~ OAK
A57. To continue in existence (even if there is no money left). ~ BE
A58. Perhaps you will not get the point of this but if you do it will stick. ~ ARROW
A60. This is against the law. (plur.) ~ REDS
A63. This fellow wears a fur coat this winter because he controlled the market in the fall. ~ BEAR
A65. Fairy-tale monsters. ~ OGRES
A67. A member of the younger set. ~ TOT
A68. Who's Whoo in night life. ~ OWL
A69. This is what Santa Claus did this summer. ~ RESTED
A71. What the rattlesnake did when it rattled. ~ WARNED
A73. The kind of relations that come between married couples. ~ ESTRANGED

D1. A member of an Indian tribe. ~ CREE
D2. Speaking of hubby, this is what she called him. ~ HE
D3. An old-style steering gear. ~ REIN
D4. This is within. ~ INTO
D5. A preposition. ~ TO
D6. The title of the latest talkie. ~ MRS
D7. These are always hanging around the zoo. ~ APES
D8. More shrinking. ~ SHIER
D9. This is what he did to the roughneck. ~ SHAVED
D10. A tooth. ~ COG
D12. This was hit hard last month. ~ ANVIL
D13. This is what she had to use for the rent. ~ NEEDLE
D16. This "fawed down and went blooey!" ~ STOCKMARKET
D18. A self-service filling station. ~ CAFETERIA
D20. This one took to the Canadian woods after a run on the bank. ~ ELK
D22. We wish you many happy returns of this kind of a day. ~ REDLETTER
D25. Depressed (after the crash.) ~ DENTED
D28. They used this to break in a new batter. ~ EGG
D29. This period comes before the end of the sentence. ~ TERM
D30. A member of the Aryan race in India. ~ HINDOO
D31. Horizontal No. 24 in a vertical position. ~ OLD
D32. A reply from Sweden. ~ YAH
D37. Something is always being done for the love of this. ~ PETE
D40. If you do this right you will make a hit. ~ AIM
D41. Many investors do this now. ~ OWE
D42. This is wild and woolly. ~ RAM
D44. When brought face to face this will tell the truth. ~ MIRROR
D48. This kind of a jest is very coarse. ~ RIBALD
D50. A deep ravine. ~ GORGE
D52. You can never get anywhere with this without pull. ~ OAR
D55. This speech was heard in Minnesota. ~ NORSE
D59. These hope to regain their spirits. ~ WETS
D61. This is pretty soft for a duck but not for a stockholder. ~ DOWN
D62. The dinner that neither Dolly nor Alice attended. ~ STAG
D63. Consult your broker about this. ~ BOND
D64. This is as meek as a lamb. ~ EWE
D66. This is a mouthful. ~ SET
D70. This one has a lot of inside information. (abbr.) ~ DR
D72. This can make a reporter out of a porter. ~ RE


